following operations on a doubly linked list?
struct Node* head = createNode(10);
head = insertEnd(head, 20);
head = insertEnd(head, 30);
head = insertAtPosition(head, 3, 25);

questions.questionText:
A doubly linked list contains 1, 2, 3, 4, 5. The following statements are executed. If  tail points to
the last node of the resulting list, what does  backwardTraversal(tail)  print?
head = delPos(head, 3);
head = delLast(head);
head = delHead(head);

