questions.questionText:
A binary tree has root 4 with a left child 2 and a right child 6 (both leaves). What is the output of
the following function when called as  trav(root)  ?
void trav(tree_pointer p)
{
if (p) {
printf("%d ", p->data);
trav(p->left_child);
trav(p->right_child);
printf("%d ", p->data);
}
}

